Here `dt` is used directly as `Mim::delay` in the tuple. So `set_use_delayed_free` returns `Mim::delay` (a tracked value but not wrapped in `Tracked<>`).

But wait - earlier `delay_enter_freeing` returned `(Tracked<Mim::delay>, Tracked<Mim::delay_actor>)` and we had to call `.0.get()`. So the return type of single-value vs multi-value transitions differs?

